<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c1deef73-762f-459a-b842-ed07b742bd03" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a3d095a4-fa45-4b3a-af9f-a0495c820309" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-solution="Add 4; 18, 22" data-solution-options="[&quot;Add 4; 18, 22&quot;, &quot;Multiply by 3; 42, 126&quot;, &quot;Multiply by 4; 56, 224&quot;, &quot;Add 3; 17, 20&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which describes the rule and the next two terms in the sequence? 2, 6, 10, 14, …</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>That’s correct! Check yourself: Subtracting consecutive terms results in the difference 4. This means you add 4 to each term to get the next term.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  
